  "application_type_full": "Listed building consent",
  "description": "This request is for retrospective consent for the replacement of my flat's front door. Unfortunately, I wasn't aware I needed consent for this work, but more than that, there are good reasons that I have already completed it in good faith. These reasons are the following:\n\n•\tThe original door had begun to expand and warp, especially in the winter. It was a problem for a while, jamming into the frame and becoming extremely difficult to open and close at times. This was a mostly a nuisance before, but it became a real problem for myself and my family when I had a child. I could not find myself locked inside and unable to open my door with a baby in the house, or in an emergency.\n•\tThere was always a draught through the seams of the door and cold air in the winter. In terms of energy efficiency, it was like I had no door. The single pane of glass did not help in this regard either. There is a larger problem on the whole western side of, I believe, every flat in the building, but the door was especially bad for retaining any heat in the cold months.\n•\tThe door and frame themselves had begun to deteriorate. I believe this was due to condensation seeping into the wood of the door (which may also have caused it to expand and not open or close with ease).\n\nOf course, I take responsibility for not knowing to apply for this prior, but as I will explain in this application with some detail, I did not see any logical reason why I should be stopped from changing my front door. If there is anything I have not explained satisfactorily, please contact me before making a decision as I would very much prefer not to have to downgrade my door once again.",
